# =============================================================================
# theme/qmldir — tells QML that these three files are SINGLETONS
# =============================================================================
# A "singleton" is a thing there is exactly one of, that anything can reach
# without being handed a reference to it. Theme, Ice and Midnight are all
# singletons because a desktop with two disagreeing copies of the palette is
# a desktop with a bug.
#
# QML will not treat a file as a singleton on the strength of the `pragma
# Singleton` line inside it alone — it also has to be listed here, in a plain
# text file, in this exact shape:
#
#     singleton <TypeName> <version> <FileName>
#
# Forget this file and the shell fails at start-up with "Ice is not a type",
# which is a confusing way to be told "you did not write it down here".
#
# This directory is pulled in by `import "../../theme"` from the components.
# =============================================================================

singleton Ice 1.0 Ice.qml
singleton Midnight 1.0 Midnight.qml
singleton Theme 1.0 Theme.qml
